      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 563986450,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Thank you for your changes, some observations:\n\n1. The changes to the existing -104 dissector seem to be mostly comments and whitespace changes with the addition of a few dissection items and don't seem to be related to IEC 60870-5-107.  As such, they should be submitted as a separate merge request.  Gratuitous white space changes should be avoided unless reformatting the entire file to comply with our whitespace suggestions and if doing so should also be a separate merge request.\n1. I'm not sure what the whitespace change to the mysql dissector is doing here.\n1. The -104-sec dissector seems to be mostly a copy of the existing -104 dissector, duplicating all the code in this way isn't maintainable.  I haven't looked in detail at what changes the -5-7 extensions make to -104, but these should either be incorporated in the existing -104 dissector (which is still called -104 by the IEC even with the extensions) or the common elements between the protocols factored out into another file so that there is no code duplication.\n1.  Multiple commits. The multiple commits seem to show a lot of work in progress and should be squashed before creating the MR.\n1. Commit message.  we have guidelines on the formatting of the ommit message, see [here](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/wikis/Development/SubmittingPatches#writing-a-good-commit-message).",
          "author": {
            "id": 6621762,
            "username": "graham.bloice",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Graham Bloice",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
