        {
          "id": 566393438,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Hi Maurizio,\n\nWhile I understand your intent to keep things separate, by including what seems to be the entirety of the existing -104 dissector as duplicate code this change would create a maintenance issue for the Wireshark team so can't be accepted as is.  FYI, there is another open MR, !2184 that adds the -7 security extensions without duplicating the -104 code.\n\nThe MR posted by you contains an irrelevant change to the mysql dissector, this can be seen on the changes tab of the MR.\n\nAs noted for the commit message, we have some information on submitting changes [here](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/wikis/Development/SubmittingPatches).",
